{"id": 28, "ts": 1781332508.609796, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fA** is the strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile we still lack direct evidence of A\u2019s stress\u2011resilience, the new information about **Candidate\u202fC**\u2014that he \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d\u2014does give C a clear advantage on that criterion. However, C\u2019s profile also includes \u201cdifficulty communicating ideas\u201d and being \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d which raise serious doubts about his crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication\u2014both essential for safe long\u2011haul operations. Compared with B, whose grumpy and uncooperative behavior is already documented, C\u2019s interpersonal concerns appear at least as severe, if not more so. Given A\u2019s proven ability to anticipate danger, understand complex connections, possess excellent spatial vision, and demonstrate very good leadership, these strengths in operational reliability, technical competence, and decision quality outweigh the unresolved stress\u2011resilience gap, especially when the alternatives have clear cooperation deficits."}
